on, and verify the robot's current location before attempting a pick.", 'When When a multi-step transport task requires moving multiple objects between locations with limited grippers and a step budget: Plan once, then execute concrete pick/move/drop actions without redundant "think" steps, using both grippers to carry two objects per trip and verifying locations before picking. After the final move, immediately drop all carried objects and confirm every target is at its destination before the step budget expires.', "When When a multi-step transport task must be completed within a limited step budget: After forming a plan, immediately execute concrete pick/move/drop actions and never emit repeated 'think' actions, since each consumes a step. Alternate one brief thought with one real action, and verify location before picking."]}
