CHIME-MAS insights: {'proposer': ["When When operating a two-gripper robot that must relocate multiple objects between two rooms within a limited step budget.: Emit concrete pick/move/drop commands immediately instead of chaining think-only steps, and use both grippers to carry two objects per trip—including planning reverse-direction objects into the return leg—to minimize trips within the limited budget. Verify only when an action's validity is genuinely uncertain, and after the final drop confirm all objects are in the target room before assuming completion.", 'When When relocating many objects between two locations with a two-gripper robot under a limited step budget.: Emit only concrete pick/move/drop commands, avoid think-only or duplicate steps, carry two objects per trip, and after the last drop verify all objects are at the target before assuming completion.'], 'checker': ["When When an agent proposes a planning or 'think' action instead of a concrete executable action that advances the task state.: Reject every 'think'/planning proposal uniformly and require the immediate concrete next action (pick/move/drop) so the task state advances; never support or let through planning chatter even when it restates a correct plan, since repeated no-ops burn the step budget.", "When When an agent proposes repeated no-op 'think' actions instead of concrete executable actions toward the goal.: Reject any 'think' proposal that repeats a prior thought without a new concrete action; require the agent to emit the actual next executable action (e.g., pick/move/drop) and only support proposals that advance the task state.", "When When an agent proposes a no-op planning or 'think' action instead of a concrete executable action that advances the task state.: Reject any 'think' or planning proposal that does not immediately precede a concrete executable action (pick/move/drop); require the agent to emit the actual next executable action so the task state advances, and never allow repeated planning chatter since it burns the step budget."], 'finalizer': ["When When a multi-step transport task requires moving objects between locations with limited step budget: After forming a plan, immediately execute concrete pick/move/drop actions rather than emitting repeated 'think' actions, since each think consumes a step. Alternate one brief thought with one real action, and verify the robot's current location before attempting a pick.", 'When When a multi-step transport task must be completed within a limited step budget and multiple objects need to be relocated between locations.: Commit to a single plan and execute only concrete pick/move/drop actions with no redundant think steps, using both grippers to carry two objects per trip and verifying locations before picking. Track every remaining object—including those already at a target or needing a reverse move—and avoid duplicate actions so all are delivered before the step budget expires.', "When When a multi-step transport task must be completed within a limited step budget: After forming a plan, immediately execute concrete pick/move/drop actions and never emit repeated 'think' actions, since each consumes a step. Alternate one brief thought with one real action, and verify location before picking."]}
