able actions toward the goal.: Reject any 'think' proposal that repeats a prior thought without a new concrete action; require the agent to emit the actual next executable action (e.g., pick/move/drop) and only support proposals that advance the task state.", "When When an agent proposes a no-op planning or 'think' action instead of a concrete executable action that advances the task state.: Reject any 'think' or planning proposal that does not immediately precede a concrete executable action (pick/move/drop); require the agent to emit the actual next executable action so the task state advances, and never allow repeated planning chatter since it burns the step budget."], 'finalizer': ["When When a multi-step transport task requires swapping or relocating many objects between two locations under a limited step budget.: Commit to one plan and execute only concrete pick/move/drop actions with minimal think steps, using both grippers to carry two objects per trip. Before each pick, verify the object's current location against the goal and track all remaining objects to avoid redundant or invalid moves.", "When When a multi-step transport task requires moving objects between locations with limited step budget: After forming a plan, immediately execute concrete pick/move/drop actions rather than emitting repeated 'think' actions, since each think consumes a step. Alternate one brief thought with one real action, and verify the robot's current location before attempting a pick.", 'When When a multi-step transport task must be completed within a limited step budget and multiple objects need to be relocated between locations.: Commit to a single plan and execute only concrete pick/move/drop actions with no redundant think steps, using both grippers to carry two objects per trip and verifying locations before picking. Track every remaining object—including those already at a target or needing a reverse move—and avoid duplicate actions so all are delivered before the step budget expires.']}
